For CE configuration of transistor,
$\begin{aligned}
& \Delta=160, R_B=4 \mathrm{ K} \Omega, R_C=4 \mathrm{ K} \Omega \\
& \therefore A_{\mathrm{V}}=\beta=\frac{R_C}{\mathrm{R}_B}=\left(\frac{\Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{C}}}{\Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{B}}}\right)\left(\frac{\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{C}}}{\mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{B}}}\right) \\
& \Rightarrow 160=\frac{\Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{C}}}{100 \times 10^{-6}} \times \frac{4}{1}
\end{aligned}\therefore$ Change in output current, $\Delta \mathrm{I}_{\mathrm{C}}=\Delta \mathrm{mA}$

